{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"files\":[{\"content\":\"#include<stdio.h>\\n#include<stdlib.h>\\n#include<string.h>\\n#include<stddef.h>\\n#include<stdint.h>\\n\\n/* Maximum size (in char) for neighbors and compute lists */\\n#define MAX 100\\n\\ntypedef struct {\\n  int id;\\n  float value;\\n  char neighbors[MAX];\\n} Node;\\n\\ntypedef struct {\\n  int *keys;\\n  int *indices;\\n  size_t capacity;\\n} IdIndex;\\n\\n/* Reads input, allocates memory, writes graph size and node list. Returns the graph. */\\nNode* read_input(char* fname, int *n, char* list) {\\n  Node* data = NULL;\\n  FILE *fl = NULL;\\n\\n  if (fname == NULL)\\n    fl = stdin;\\n  else\\n    fl = fopen(fname, \\\"r\\\");\\n\\n  if (fl == NULL) {\\n    fprintf(stderr, \\\"Error!\\\\n\\\");\\n    exit(1);\\n  }\\n\\n  // header\\n  fscanf(fl, \\\"%d %[^\\n]\\\", n, list);\\n\\n  if (*n > 0) {\\n    data = (Node*) malloc ((*n)*sizeof(Node));\\n    if(data == NULL){\\n      fprintf(stderr, \\\"Error!\\\\n\\\");\\n      exit(1);\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  for(int i = 0; i < *n; i++)\\n    fscanf(fl, \\\"%d %f %[^\\n]\\\", &data[i].id, &data[i].value, data[i].neighbors);\\n\\n  fclose(fl);\\n  return data;\\n}\\n\\n/* Mix an integer ID before masking it into the power-of-two table. */\\nstatic size_t hash_id(int id) {\\n  uint32_t x = (uint32_t)id;\\n  x ^= x >> 16;\\n  x *= UINT32_C(0x7feb352d);\\n  x ^= x >> 15;\\n  x *= UINT32_C(0x846ca68b);\\n  x ^= x >> 16;\\n  return (size_t)x;\\n}\\n\\n/* Build an open-addressed index; retaining the first occurrence matches the old scan. */\\nstatic void build_id_index(IdIndex *index, const Node *g, int size) {\\n  index->keys = NULL;\\n  index->indices = NULL;\\n  index->capacity = 0;\\n\\n  if (size <= 0)\\n    return;\\n\\n  size_t max_size = (size_t)-1;\\n  size_t count = (size_t)size;\\n  if (count > max_size / 2) {\\n    fprintf(stderr, \\\"Error!\\\\n\\\");\\n    exit(1);\\n  }\\n  size_t needed = count * 2;\\n  size_t capacity = 1;\\n  while (capacity < needed) {\\n    if (capacity > max_size / 2) {\\n      fprintf(stderr, \\\"Error!\\\\n\\\");\\n      exit(1);\\n    }\\n    capacity *= 2;\\n  }\\n  if (capacity > max_size / sizeof(int)) {\\n    fprintf(stderr, \\\"Error!\\\\n\\\");\\n    exit(1);\\n  }\\n\\n  index->keys = (int*)malloc(capacity * sizeof(int));\\n  index->indices = (int*)malloc(capacity * sizeof(int));\\n  if (index->keys == NULL || index->indices == NULL) {\\n    fprintf(stderr, \\\"Error!\\\\n\\\");\\n    exit(1);\\n  }\\n  index->capacity = capacity;\\n\\n  for (size_t i = 0; i < capacity; i++)\\n    index->indices[i] = -1;\\n\\n  size_t mask = capacity - 1;\\n  for (int i = 0; i < size; i++) {\\n    size_t slot = hash_id(g[i].id) & mask;\\n    while (index->indices[slot] != -1 && index->keys[slot] != g[i].id)\\n      slot = (slot + 1) & mask;\\n    if (index->indices[slot] == -1) {\\n      index->keys[slot] = g[i].id;\\n      index->indices[slot] = i;\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/* Returns the first index of the node with the given ID, or -1 if absent. */\\nstatic int find_by_id(const IdIndex *index, int id) {\\n  if (index->capacity == 0)\\n    return -1;\\n\\n  size_t mask = index->capacity - 1;\\n  size_t slot = hash_id(id) & mask;\\n  while (index->indices[slot] != -1) {\\n    if (index->keys[slot] == id)\\n      return index->indices[slot];\\n    slot = (slot + 1) & mask;\\n  }\\n  return -1;\\n}\\n\\n/* Computes the sum for the node with the given id */\\nfloat get_costly(Node *g, int id, const IdIndex *index) {\\n  char *t;\\n  int idmax = -1;\\n  float max = 0;\\n  char *auxptr;\\n\\n  int nd = find_by_id(index, id);\\n  if(nd < 0)\\n    return max;\\n\\n  char aux[MAX];\\n  strcpy(aux, g[nd].neighbors);\\n  t = strtok_r(aux, \\\" \\\", &auxptr);\\n\\n  do {\\n    int neighbor_id = atoi(t);\\n    int d = find_by_id(index, neighbor_id);\\n    if (d >= 0 && max < g[d].value) {\\n      max = g[d].value;\\n      idmax = neighbor_id;\\n    }\\n  } while ((t = strtok_r(NULL, \\\" \\\", &auxptr)));\\n\\n  float r = g[nd].value;\\n\\n  if(idmax != -1)\\n    r += get_costly(g, idmax, index);\\n\\n  return (r);\\n}\\n\\n/* Main program - calls read input, computes sum for each node in the list, prints output */\\nint main() {\\n  char *fileN = NULL;\\n  char computelist[MAX];\\n  int n = -1;\\n  Node* input = NULL;\\n\\n  input = read_input(fileN, &n, computelist);\\n  IdIndex index;\\n  build_id_index(&index, input, n);\\n\\n  // process\\n  for(char *c = strtok(computelist, \\\" \\\"); c != NULL; c = strtok(NULL, \\\" \\\"))\\n    printf(\\\"%s: %f\\\\n\\\", c, get_costly(input, atoi(c), &index));\\n\\n  free(index.keys);\\n  free(index.indices);\\n  free(input);\\n  return 0;\\n}\\n\",\"path\":\"src/graph.c\"}],\"hypothesis\":\"An open-addressed hash index built once will replace repeated linear ID scans with expected constant-time lookups, reducing lookup work during recursive traversal while preserving first-match behavior for duplicate IDs.\",\"notes\":\"This isolates ID lookup: traversal order, neighbor selection, float accumulation, and output formatting are retained. The index stores the first node for each ID and is reused by all recursive and top-level lookups. No performance or correctness measurements were run.\",\"research\":{\"queries\":[],\"urls\":[]},\"sources_kept\":[],\"transformations\":[\"Build a power-of-two open-addressed hash table once after input parsing and use it for node-ID lookup.\",\"Insert only the first node for each ID so duplicate IDs retain the original linear scan's first-match semantics.\",\"Reuse the index throughout recursive traversal and release its allocations before exit.\",\"Allocate the node array when n is one, as well as for larger positive sizes.\"]}"}}
